      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a very brave thing to admit how much you're struggling, even when everything looks perfect from the outside. That grayness you feel is a heavy weight, and you don't have to carry it pretending to be fine anymore. Sometimes the quietest, most profound emptiness is the one that needs the most attention, and it's okay to let it take up space. If you're tired of the performance, maybe it's time to find a way to just *be* with the exhaustion.",
